/* src/facts/walk_arms.def — THE RESTORED ARMS of the necessary-run walk: the
 * test-only lever rows of the walk-parameter table (docs/design/span_arms.md
 * §3.7, T7's `restored arms` row; ruled at review 2026-11-08 r2 S9).
 *
 * A restored arm runs one arm of `src/facts/req.c`'s walk in its form BEFORE
 * the unit that changed it, so `make test-axes` can sweep the old form against
 * the new one (an answer-identity arm, `tests/axes/run_axes.sh`'s internal
 * arms). It is reachable only from `build/pcrec-harness`
 * (`--harness=restore=NAME[+NAME...]`, `PcrecHarnessOptions.walk_arms`), never
 * from a caller: the units it restores can only change speed through pick rows
 * that carry their own denies (span_arms §3.7 "The rule"), so no public bit.
 *
 *   WALK_ARM(ID, name, facts)
 *
 *   ID     `PCREC_WALK_ARM(ID)` is the arm's bit.
 *   name   its spelling, in `--harness=restore=` and in the `--emit-facts`
 *          token `harness:<name>[+<name>...]` (facts_listing.md §4.1.3¶4a).
 *   facts  the walk OUTPUTS the arm can change, a mask of `PfFactId` bits
 *          (`PatFacts.have`'s layout). A fact derived
 *          from one of them inherits the token through its ask
 *          (`src/facts/facts.c` `pf_ask`), so only the walk's own facts are
 *          listed here.
 *
 * One row per restorable arm. `empty` is span_arms unit E1's (T2 row 1, a
 * repeat of a width-0 body: the old min-0 gap and best-only copy) and E2's T3
 * row E-1 (an `A_EMPTY` node: the old CUT). `zero` is unit E2's (T3 rows E-4
 * and E-5, a node other than the empty string that consumes nothing: an assertion, `\G`,
 * `\K`, a check callout, a lookaround of either lowering, back to the old
 * CUT). `rep` is unit R1's (T2 rows 2-3, a repeat of a body that consumes:
 * the old best-only copy and gap). `tie` is R1's rarity tie rule (the run choice's rows 2-4). A later unit adds its own row (L1 `look`). */
WALK_ARM(EMPTY, "empty", (1u << PF_REQ_WHOLE_RUN) | (1u << PF_REQ_PIECES))
/* span_arms E2 (T3 E-4, E-5 as the plain unit) */
WALK_ARM(ZERO,  "zero",  (1u << PF_REQ_WHOLE_RUN) | (1u << PF_REQ_PIECES))

/* span_arms unit R1 ([REPEAT-RUN], T2 rows 2-3, the power arm): a repeat of
 * a body that consumes, read as its copies. Restored: today's best-only copy
 * (`m >= 1`) and the gap (`m = 0`, `X{0}` included). */
WALK_ARM(REP,   "rep",   (1u << PF_REQ_WHOLE_RUN) | (1u << PF_REQ_PIECES))

/* span_arms unit R1's tie rule (`rn_choice_rows`, D191): at equal information
 * the rarer run, then the nearer, then content order. Restored: the
 * predecessor's choice, information and then the first run. */
WALK_ARM(TIE,   "tie",   (1u << PF_REQ_WHOLE_RUN) | (1u << PF_REQ_PIECES))
#undef WALK_ARM
